# Pinned revision of the SECOND cross-repo counterpart: libviprs/libviprs-cli
# (the `viprs` CLI binary the vips-differential suite builds and runs).
#
# This is the sibling of COUNTERPART_REV. COUNTERPART_REV pins the core
# `libviprs` crate this suite depends on as a path-dependency; CLI_COUNTERPART_REV
# pins the `libviprs-cli` crate the CLI-DIFFERENTIAL harness (tests/common/cli.rs)
# shells out to. The morphology differential cell (tests/cli_morphology_diff.rs)
# runs `viprs <op> ...` on a committed input and decode-compares its output
# against committed vips 8.18.4 references, so it must build the CLI at a
# KNOWN revision — not "whatever happens to be checked out".
#
# CI behaviour: the `cli-differential` job checks libviprs-cli out at EXACTLY
# this commit next to the core checkout (../libviprs-cli), the same
# no-branch-guessing / no-silent-fallback discipline COUNTERPART_REV enforces
# for core (issue #58). The first non-comment, non-blank line below is the
# authoritative 40-char SHA; the trailing comment is a human label only.
#
# LOCAL behaviour: a local run does NOT clone. tests/common/cli.rs builds
# whatever `../libviprs-cli` (or $VIPRS_CLI_DIR) physically is, and honours a
# pre-built `$VIPRS_BIN` override. So on a developer machine the harness tests
# the working tree of the sibling CLI, and this pin only governs CI.
#
# Four-repo pin-bump order (CLI_CONTRACT.md §7): core -> cli -> org -> tests.
# To bump: set this to a libviprs-cli commit SHA, rerun
# `cargo test --test cli_morphology_diff` against the sibling checkout, and
# update the label comment below.
